MPTY, X, O = 0, 1, 2\nNAME = {X: \"X\", O: \"O\"}\nLINES = ((0,1,2),(3,4,5),(6,7,8),(0,3,6),(1,4,7),(2,5,8),(0,4,8),(2,4,6))\n\ndef other(p): return O if p == X else X\n\ndef mono(b, p):\n    return any(b[a]==p and b[c]==p and b[d]==p for a,c,d in LINES)\n\ndef anyfull(b):\n    return any(b[a]!=EMPTY and b[c]!=EMPTY and b[d]!=EMPTY for a,c,d in LINES)\n\ndef full(b): return all(c!=EMPTY for c in b)\n\n# --- rule terminal functions: return winner or None ---\ndef rA(b,last):\n    if mono(b,X): return X\n    if mono(b,O): return O\n    return last if full(b) else None\n\ndef rB(b,last):\n    if mono(b,X): return X\n    if mono(b,O): return O\n    return other(last) if full(b) else None\n\ndef rC(b,last):   # misere, fill -> last mover wins\n    if mono(b,last): return other(last)\n    if mono(b,other(last)): return last  # unreachable in play; defensive\n    return last if full(b) else None\n\ndef rD(b,last):\n    if mono(b,last): return other(last)\n    if mono(b,other(last)): return last\n    return other(last) if full(b) else None\n\ndef rE(b,last):\n    return last if anyfull(b) else None\n\ndef rG(b,last):   # Maker-breaker: X wins by X line; O wins a filled board with no X line\n    if mono(b,X): return X\n    return O if full(b) else None\n```\n\nWait, rC: `if mono(b,other(last)): return last` — this case is \"opponent has a line but it's not last mover's stone\". In play, before last's move there was no line, so any line includes last's stone → mono(b,last) would be true. So the defensive branch is unreachable. But careful: in rD/rC, after the last move, could BOTH players have lines? Only if a line existed before, impossible. OK. But also in the DFS we call rule on non-terminal states too, and rule must not declare terminal for states with an old line... In our DFS, children always have last = the mover. So consistent.\n\nHmm, but there's an issue: for root of F, the pre-placed O at 4: we call rec(b, X, 0) where b has O at 4, no line. Inside rec, `last = othe