`len_dist[stones(b)-s0] += 1` at terminal. Good, cheap.\n\nLet me finalize.\n\nAlso: printing raw output later — I'll run `python3 solver.py > output.txt` and embed both.\n\nLet me write the file now via the write tool. Then run. Then searches.\n\nOne concern: `@lru_cache` on nested function `rec` with tuple keys — fine.\n\nPerformance of greedy with Fraction: per state doing rule checks for each move (cheap). Total states ~6000 × 9 moves × opponent threat check (9) — ~500k rule calls, fine.\n\nLet me write.\n\nActually, also need `import sys` maybe not. Skip unused imports.\n\nLet me write the full script text.\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nno_draw_ttt.py -- exhaustive solvers for 3x3 tic-tac-toe no-draw rule sets.\n\nStandard library only. Every number printed by this script is obtained by\nenumerating the complete game tree (every legal sequence of moves, stopping\nat terminal positions). Nothing is sampled.\n\nCell numbering:\n    0 1 2\n    3 4 5\n    6 7 8\nX moves first (rule F excepted: O is pre-placed on the centre).\n\nEach rule is a function (board, last_mover) -> (terminal?, winner|None).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\nEMPTY, X, O = 0, 1, 2\nSYM = {X: \"X\", O: \"O\", None: \"draw\"}\n\n\ndef other(p):\n    return O if p == X else X\n\n\nLINES = ((0, 1, 2), (3, 4, 5), (6, 7, 8),\n         (0, 3, 6), (1, 4, 7), (2, 5, 8),\n         (0, 4, 8), (2, 4, 6))\n\n\ndef mono(b, p):\n    return any(b[a] == p and c == p and b[d] == p for a, c, d in LINES)\n```\ncareful: `c` shadows... write properly:\n\n```python\ndef mono(b, p):\n    return any(b[i] == p and b[j] == p and b[k] == p for i, j, k in LINES)\n\n\ndef any_full_line(b):\n    return any(b[i] != EMPTY and b[j] != EMPTY and b[k] != EMPTY for i, j, k in LINES)\n\n\ndef board_full(b):\n    return all(c != EMPTY for c in b)\n\n\ndef nstones(b):\n    return sum(1 for c in b if c != EMPTY)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Terminal rules: (board, last_mover) -> (terminal?, winner or None)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef R_standard_draw(b, last):\n    \"\"\"Classic tic-tac-toe: a lineless full board is a draw.\"\"\"\n    if mono(b, X):\n        return True, X\n    if mono(b, O):\n        return True, O\n    if board_full(b):\n        return True, None\n    return False, None\n\n\ndef R_standard_fill_wins(b, last):\n    \"\"\"Rule A: standard lines; full board with no line -> last mover wins.\"\"\"\n    if mono(b, X):\n        return True, X\n    if mono(b, O):\n        return True, O\n    if board_full(b):\n        return True, last\n    return False, None\n\n\ndef R_standard_fill_loses(b, last):\n    \"\"\"Rule B: standard lines; full board with no line -> last mover loses.\"\"\"\n    if mono(b, X):\n        return True, X\n    if mono(b, O):\n        return True, O\n    if board_full(b):\n        return True, other(last)\n    return False, None\n\n\ndef R_misere_fill_wins(b, last):\n    \"\"\"Rule C: completing your own line loses; full board -> last mover wins.\"\"\"\n    if mono(b, last):\n        return True, other(last)\n    if mono(b, other(last)):        # unreachable in play; defensive\n        return True, last\n    if board_full(b):\n        return True, last\n    return False, None\n\n\ndef R_misere_fill_loses(b, last):\n    \"\"\"Rule D: completing your own line loses; full board -> last mover loses.\"\"\"\n    if mono(b, last):\n        return True, other(last)\n    if mono(b, other(last)):        # unreachable in play; defensive\n        return True, last\n    if board_full(b):\n        return True, other(last)\n    return False, None\n\n\ndef R_any_line(b, last):\n    \"\"\"Rule E: any move making a line fully occupied wins, regardless of symbol.\"\"\"\n    if any_full_line(b):\n        return True, last\n    return False, None\n\n\ndef R_maker_breaker(b, last):\n    \"\"\"Rule G (Maker-Breaker): X wins by an X line; O wins a filled board with no X line.\"\"\"\n    if mono(b, X):\n        return True, X\n    if board_full(b):\n        return True, O\n    return False, None\n```\n\nThen solve.\n\n```python\nEMPTY9 = (EMPTY,) * 9\nF_START = (EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY, O, EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY)\n\n\ndef value_function(rule):\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def value(b, turn):\n        term, w = rule(b, other(turn))\n        if term:\n            return w\n        vals = set()\n        for i in range(9):\n            if b[i] == EMPTY:\n                vals.add(value(b[:i] + (turn,) + b[i + 1:], other(turn)))\n        if turn in vals:\n            return turn\n        if None in vals:\n            return None\n        return other(turn)\n    return value\n\n\ndef solve(rule, start=EMPTY9, start_turn=X):\n    s0 = nstones(start)\n    value = value_function(rule)\n    ev = value(start, start_turn)     # not needed but harmless; skip? remove\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def rec(b, turn):\n        term, w = rule(b, other(turn))\n        if term:\n            L = nstones(b) - s0\n            counts = {X: 0, O: 0, None: 0}\n            counts[w] = 1\n            probs = {X: Fraction(0), O: Fraction(0), None: Fraction(0)}\n            probs[w] = Fraction(1)\n            return counts, L, L, probs, Fraction(L), 1\n        legal = [i for i in range(9) if b[i] == EMPTY]\n        m = len(legal)\n        counts = {X: 0, O: 0, None: 0}\n        probs = {X: Fraction(0), O: Fraction(0), None: Fraction(0)}\n        mx = 0\n        slen = 0\n        elen = Fraction(0)\n        nstates = 0\n        for i in legal:\n            nb = b[:i] + (turn,) + b[i + 1:]\n            assert nstones(nb) == nstones(b) + 1\n            c2, m2, s2, p2, e2, n2 = rec(nb, other(turn))\n            for k2 in counts:\n                counts[k2] += c2[k2]\n            mx = max(mx, m2)\n            slen += s2\n            elen += e2 / m\n            nstates += n2\n            for k2 in probs:\n                probs[k2] += p2[k2] / m\n        return counts, mx, slen, probs, elen, nstates + 1\n\n    counts, max_len, sum_len, prob, exp_len, nstates = rec(start, start_turn)\n    total = counts[X] + counts[O] + counts[None]\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def greedy(b, turn):\n        term, w = rule(b, other(turn))\n        if term:\n            L = nstones(b) - s0\n            counts_ = {X: 0, O: 0, None: 0}\n            counts_[w] = 1\n            probs_ = {X: Fraction(0), O: Fraction(0), None: Fraction(0)}\n            probs_[w] = Fraction(1)\n            return counts_, L, Fraction(L), probs_\n\n        def play(bb, i, p):\n            return bb[:i] + (p,) + bb[i + 1:]\n\n        legal = [i for i in range(9) if b[i] == EMPTY]\n        wins = []\n        for i in legal:\n            term2, w2 = rule(play(b, i, turn), turn)\n            if term2 and w2 == turn:\n                wins.append(i)\n        if wins:\n            cand = wins\n        else:\n            opp = other(turn)\n            safe = []\n            for i in legal:\n                nb = play(b, i, turn)\n                term2, w2 = rule(nb, turn)\n                if term2:\n                    continue\n                threat = False\n                for j in range(9):\n                    if nb[j] == EMPTY:\n                        term3, w3 = rule(play(nb, j, opp), opp)\n                        if term3 and w3 == opp:\n                            threat = True\n                            break\n                if not threat:\n                    safe.append(i)\n            cand = safe if safe else legal\n        m = len(cand)\n        counts_ = {X: 0, O: 0, None: 0}\n        probs_ = {X: Fraction(0), O: Fraction(0), None: Fraction(0)}\n        exp_ = Fraction(0)\n        mx_ = 0\n        for i in cand:\n            c2, m2, e2, p2 = greedy(play(b, i, turn), other(turn))\n            for k2 in counts_:\n                counts_[k2] += c2[k2]\n            for k2 in probs_:\n                probs_[k2] += p2[k2] / m\n            exp_ += e2 / m\n            mx_ = max(mx_, m2)\n        return counts_, mx_, exp_, probs_\n\n    gcounts, gmax, gexp, gprob = greedy(start, start_turn)\n\n    first_values = {}\n    for i in range(9):\n        if start[i] == EMPTY:\n            first_values[i] = value(start[:i] + (start_turn,) + start[i + 1:],\n                                   other(start_turn))\n\n    return {\n        \"counts\": counts, \"total\": total, \"max_len\": max_len,\n        \"mean_len\": Fraction(sum_len, total), \"exp_len\": exp_len,\n        \"prob\": prob, \"states\": nstates,\n        \"value\": value(start, start_turn),\n        \"first_values\": first_values,\n        \"winning_first\": sorted(i for i, v in first_values.items() if v == start_turn),\n        \"greedy_counts\": gcounts, \"greedy_max\": gmax, \"greedy_mean\": gexp,\n        \"greedy_prob\": gprob,\n    }\n```\n\nWait: there's a bug in rec's leaf: `counts[w] = 1` with w=None works because None is a key. Good.\n\nBug risk: `value(start, start_turn)` — for F start, rule(start, other(X)=O): no mono, not full → (False, None) → fine.\n\nNow the standard extras and print functions.\n\n```python\ndef fmt_pct(fr):\n    return f\"{float(fr) * 100:.3f}%\"\n\n\ndef print_report(name, rule, start, start_turn, note):\n    r = solve(rule, start, start_turn)\n    c, t, p = r[\"counts\"], r[\"total\"], r[\"prob\"]\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\n    print(name)\n    if note:\n        print(\"  note:\", note)\n    print(f\"  terminal lines of play (leaves) ... {t}\")\n    print(f\"  X / O / draw leaves ............... {c[X]} / {c[O]} / {c[None]}\")\n    print(f\"  leaf shares ....................... X {100*c[X]/t:.3f}%  O {100*c[O]/t:.3f}%  draw {100*c[None]/t:.3f}%\")\n    print(f\"  uniform-random-play probabilities . X {fmt_pct(p[X])}  O {fmt_pct(p[O])}  draw {fmt_pct(p[None])}\")\n    print(f\"  game length: max {r['max_len']}, mean over leaves {float(r['mean_len']):.4f}, uniform expectation {float(r['exp_len']):.4f}\")\n    print(f\"  perfect play ...................... {SYM[r['value']]}\" + (f\"; winning first moves {r['winning_first']}\" if r[\"winning_first\"] else \"; no winning first move\"))\n    gp, gc = r[\"greedy_prob\"], r[\"greedy_counts\"]\n    print(f\"  greedy policy probabilities ....... X {fmt_pct(gp[X])}  O {fmt_pct(gp[O])}  draw {fmt_pct(gp[None])}\"\n          f\"   (greedy leaves X {gc[X]} / O {gc[O]} / draw {gc[None]})\")\n    print(f\"  greedy length: max {r['greedy_max']}, expectation {float(r['greedy_mean']):.4f}\")\n    print(f\"  reachable (board, turn) states .... {r['states']}\")\n    return r\n```\n\nThen main printing all rules, plus extras.\n\nExtras:\n\n```python\ndef standard_details():\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\n    print(\"STANDARD BASELINE DETAIL (own line wins; lineless full board = draw)\")\n    term_counts = {}\n    len_dist = {}\n    def dfs(b, turn):\n        term, w = R_standard_draw(b, other(turn))\n        if term:\n            term_counts[b] = term_counts.get(b, 0) + 1\n            L = nstones(b)\n            len_dist[L] = len_dist.get(L, 0) + 1\n            return\n        for i in range(9):\n            if b[i] == EMPTY:\n                dfs(b[:i] + (turn,) + b[i + 1:], other(turn))\n    dfs(EMPTY9, X)\n    total = sum(term_counts.values())\n    print(f\"  total terminal sequences: {total}\")\n    xb = sum(1 for b, n in term_counts.items() if mono(b, X))\n    ob = sum(1 for b, n in term_counts.items() if mono(b, O))\n    both = sum(1 for b in term_counts if mono(b, X) and mono(b, O))\n    lnl = sum(1 for b in term_counts if board_full(b) and not mono(b, X) and not mono(b, O))\n    print(f\"  distinct terminal boards: {len(term_counts)}  (X-line {xb}, O-line {ob}, lineless full {lnl}, both {both})\")\n    print(f\"  length distribution (length:sequences): {dict(sorted(len_dist.items()))}\")\n    # all full boards\n    full_boards = list(combinations(range(9), 5))\n    no_line = []\n    for xs in full_boards:\n        b = [O] * 9\n        for i in xs:\n            b[i] = X\n        b = tuple(b)\n        if not mono(b, X) and not mono(b, O):\n            no_line.append(b)\n    print(f\"  all full boards 5X/4O: {len(full_boards)}; with at least one line: {len(full_boards)-len(no_line)}; lineless: {len(no_line)}\")\n    print(\"  the lineless full boards and how many terminal sequences end on each:\")\n    for b in sorted(no_line, key=lambda bb: term_counts.get(bb, 0), reverse=True):\n        grid = \"/\".join(\"\".join(\".XO\"[c] for c in b[r*3:r*3+3]) for r in range(3))\n        n = term_counts.get(b, 0)\n        print(f\"    {grid}   sequences={n}   reachable={n>0}\")\n    print(f\"  every lineless full board reachable in normal play: {all(term_counts.get(b,0)>0 for b in no_line)}\")\n```\n\nNote: `terms_counts` only includes reachable terminal boards; if a no-line board weren't reachable, `term_counts.get` = 0.\n\nAlso compute the count of full boards with a line = 110. And note that X-line/O-line terminal boards are not necessarily full.\n\nAlso distinct reachable (board, turn) states for standard: from solve()[\"states\"] (I'll capture and print there, but standard_details could print it too). I'll just rely on the A report (same tree).\n\nSwap check:\n\n```python\ndef swap_check(name, rule):\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\n    print(f\"SWAP / PIE RULE CHECK: {name}\")\n    print(\"  First player places one stone at cell c; second may swap (take that stone\")\n    print(\"  and hand the move back) or play on. 'no swap' value is the winner from\")\n    print(\"  (board={c:X}, O to move); 'swap' value from (board={c:O}, X to move).\")\n    value = value_function(rule)\n    all_second = True\n    rows = []\n    for c in range(9):\n        b_no = tuple(X if i == c else EMPTY for i in range(9))\n        b_sw = tuple(O if i == c else EMPTY for i in range(9))\n        v_no = value(b_no, O)\n        v_sw = value(b_sw, X)\n        second_wins = (v_no == O) or (v_sw == O)\n        all_second &= second_wins\n        rows.append((c, SYM[v_no], SYM[v_sw], second_wins))\n    for c, v_no, v_sw, w in rows:\n        print(f\"    c={c}: O plays on -> {v_no}; O swaps -> {v_sw}; O can force a win: {w}\")\n    print(f\"  second player wins with the swap rule for every opening: {all_second}\")\n```\nNote: for rule A, v_sw is \"value of position with O owning c, X to move\" — if that equals O, the swapper (O) wins. Good. Careful: after X opens at c and O swaps, O owns c and it's X's turn. Yes.\n\nAlso maybe do swap for B. Fine, do A and B.\n\nMain:\n```python\ndef main():\n    rules = [...]\n    summary = []\n    for name, rule, start, turn, note in rules:\n        r = print_report(name, rule, start, turn, note)\n        summary.append((name, r))\n    standard_details()\n    swap_check(\"rule A (standard + fill -> last mover wins)\", R_standard_fill_wins)\n    swap_check(\"rule B (standard + fill -> last mover loses)\", R_standard_fill_loses)\n```\n\nHmm, do I need summary table? The print_report already prints everything. A compact summary at the end is nice but the Markdown table can be built from the outputs by me. Skip extra summary print to keep output smaller. Actually maybe a compact table helps me verify; I'll build manually.\n\nLet me also add: verify rule B last-mover parity claim: print for A: \"full board => 9 stones => last mover X\". I can derive in note.\n\nNow, about run time: solve() runs rec + greedy + value for each of 9 configurations. rec Fraction probabilities: for standard tree ~550k nodes but memoized ~6k states; each state sums fractions over children — fine. greedy ~6k states × Fraction; fine. value ~6k states. DFS standard_details traverses 255k leaves with Python recursion — 550k calls, fine. Total < 10 s.\n\nOne risk: Fraction denominators in `prob` for deep states: e.g., states near the root sum many fractions; denominators lcm of products of branch factors up to 9·8·7·6·5·4·3·2 = 362,8