}}]({{subColumn.links}})\n\n [](/jdg)\n\n[Advanced Search](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\nAll Title Author Keyword Abstract DOI Classify Address Funds\n\n   \n\n-   []({{newsColumn.links}})\n    1.  [{{subColumn.name}}]({{subColumn.links}})\n\n[\n\nJournal of Dynamics and Games\n\n](/jdg)\n\n    \n\n[Advanced Search](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n-   [{{newsColumn.name}}]({{newsColumn.links}})\n    1.  [{{subColumn.name}}]({{subColumn.links}})\n-   [Home](https://www.aimsciences.org/)\n\n-   [PDF](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n-   [Cite](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n-   Share\n    \n    ![](/style/web/images/custom/share_facebook.png)\n    \n    ![](/style/web/images/custom/share_twitter.png)\n    \n    ![](/style/web/images/custom/share_linkin.png)\n    \n    ![](/style/web/images/custom/share_mendeley.png)\n    \n    ![](/style/web/images/custom/share_researchGate.png)\n    \n\n[This issue](/jdg/article/2017/4/3) [Previous Article](javascript:void\\(0\\);) [Next Article](/article/doi/10.3934/jdg.2017012)\n\nAll Title Author Keyword Abstract DOI Category Address Fund    \n\nArticle Contents![](/style/web/images/custom/icon_toright.png)\n\n[](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n\n![](/style/web/images/custom/icon_toleft.png) Article Contents\n\n[2017, Volume 4](/jdg/archive), [Issue 3](/jdg/article/2017/4/3): 191-194. Doi: [10.3934/jdg.2017011](https://doi.org/10.3934/jdg.2017011)\n\n[This issue](/jdg/article/2017/4/3) [Previous Article](javascript:void\\(0\\);) [Next Article](/article/doi/10.3934/jdg.2017012) A note on differential games with Pareto-optimal NASH equilibria: Deterministic and stochastic models†\n\n[\n\nPDF  view\n\n\n\n](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n# On Zermelo's theorem\n\n-   [Rabah Amir](javascript:void\\(0\\);)[1](javascript:void\\(0\\);), [](javascript:void\\(0\\); \"Corresponding Author: Rabah Amir, rabah-amir@uiowa.edu\"), [](mailto:rabah-amir@uiowa.edu \"mailto: rabah-amir@uiowa.edu\")  and \n-   [Igor V. Evstigneev](javascript:void\\(0\\);)[2](javascript:void\\(0\\);), [](mailto:igor.evstigneev@manchester.ac.uk \"mailto: igor.evstigneev@manchester.ac.uk\") \n\n-   1.\n    \n    Department of Economics, University of Iowa, Iowa City, IA 52242-1994, USA\n    \n-   2.\n    \n    Department of Economics, University of Manchester, Oxford Road, Manchester, M13 9PL, UK\n    \n\n-   \\* Corresponding author\n    \n    \\* Corresponding author \n\n**Received:**  February 2017\n\n**Revised:**  February 2017\n\n**Published online:**  April 2017\n\n[Abstract / Introduction](javascript:void\\(0\\);) [Full Text(HTML)](https://www.aimsciences.org/article/noLoginPage?id=6ec22007-b4e5-49f1-a59a-153cf9f1c420&journalPublisherId=jdg&type=HTML) [Related Papers](javascript:void\\(0\\);) [Cited by](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n[Abstract](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n-   ### Abstract\n    \n    A famous result in game theory known as Zermelo's theorem says that ''in chess either White can force a win, or Black can force a win, or both sides can force at least a draw\". The present paper extends this result to the class of all finite-stage two-player games of complete information with alternating moves. It is shown that in any such game either the first player has a winning strategy, or the second player has a winning strategy, or both have unbeatable strategies.\n    \n    **Keywords:**-   [Games of complete information](javascript:void\\(0\\);),\n    -   [combinatorial game theory](javascript:void\\(0\\);),\n    -   [dynamic games](javascript:void\\(0\\);),\n    -   [determinacy](javascript:void\\(0\\);),\n    -   [Zermelo's theorem](javascript:void\\(0\\);).\n    \n    **Mathematics Subject Classification:** Primary: 91A44; Secondary: 91A46, 91A25.\n    \n    **Citation:**\n    \n    ![shu](/style/web/images/article/shu.png)\n    \n    \\\\begin{equation} \\\\\\\\ \\\\end{equation}\n    \n\n[Full Text(HTML)](https://www.aimsciences.org/article/noLoginPage?id=6ec22007-b4e5-49f1-a59a-153cf9f1c420&journalPublisherId=jdg&type=HTML)\n\n-   ![加载中](/style/web/images/article/1.gif)\n\n[Related Papers](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n[Cited by](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n[References](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n-   ### References\n    \n    \\[1\\]\n    \n    [R. Amir](https://scholar.google.com/scholar?btnG=&hl=en&as_sdt=0%2C23&q=author:R. Amir), [I. V. Evstigneev](https://scholar.google.com/scholar?btnG=&hl=en&as_sdt=0%2C23&q=author:I. V. Evstigneev) and [K. R. Schenk-Hoppé](https://scholar.google.com/scholar?btnG=&hl=en&as_sdt=0%2C23&q=author:K. R. Schenk-Hoppé), Asset market games of survival: A synthesis of evolutionary and dynamic games, *Annals of Finance*, **9** (2013), 121-144.  doi: [10.1007/s10436-012-0210-5.![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/crossref.jpg \"CrossRef\")](http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s10436-012-0210-5) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/math-review.gif \"math-review\")](https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=MR3055417&return=pdf) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Asset+market+games+of+survival:+A+synthesis+of+evolutionary+and+dynamic+games+R. Amir+2013 \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n    \\[2\\]\n    \n    R. J. Aumann, *Lectures on Game Theory*, Westview, Boulder, 1989. [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=R.+J.+Aumann,++Lectures+on+Game+Theory,+Westview,+Boulder,+1989. + \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n    \\[3\\]\n    \n    [E. Borel](https://scholar.google.com/scholar?btnG=&hl=en&as_sdt=0%2C23&q=author:E. Borel), La théorie du jeu et les équations intégrales á noyau symétrique, *Comptes Rendus de l'Académie des Sciences*, **173** (1921), 1304-1308.  doi: [10.2307/1906946.![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/crossref.jpg \"CrossRef\")](http://dx.doi.org/10.2307/1906946) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/math-review.gif \"math-review\")](https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=MR0052751&return=pdf) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=La+théorie+du+jeu+et+les+équations+intégrales+á+noyau+symétrique+E. Borel+1921 \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n    \\[4\\]\n    \n    C. L. Bouton, Nim, a game with a complete mathematical theory, Annals of Mathematics, 3 (1901/02), 35-39. doi: [10.2307/1967631.![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/crossref.jpg \"CrossRef\")](http://dx.doi.org/10.2307/1967631) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/math-review.gif \"math-review\")](https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=MR1502275&return=pdf) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=C.+L.+Bouton,+Nim,+a+game+with+a+complete+mathematical+theory,+Annals+of+Mathematics,+3+\\(1901/02\\),+35-39. + \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n    \\[5\\]\n    \n    A. Kechris, *Classical Descriptive Set Theory*, Springer-Verlag, New York, 1995. doi: [10.1007/978-1-4612-4190-4.![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/crossref.jpg \"CrossRef\")](http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-4190-4) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/math-review.gif \"math-review\")](https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=MR1321597&return=pdf) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=A.+Kechris,++Classical+Descriptive+Set+Theory,+Springer-Verlag,+New+York,+1995. + \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n    \\[6\\]\n    \n    Yu. Khomskii, Intensive Course on Infinite Games, Sofia University, 2010. Available from: [https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/khomskii/infinitegames2010/InfiniteGamesSofia.pdf](https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/khomskii/infinitegames2010/InfiniteGamesSofia.pdf). [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Yu.+Khomskii,+Intensive+Course+on+Infinite+Games,+Sofia+University,+2010.+Available+from:+https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/khomskii/infinitegames2010/InfiniteGamesSofia.pdf. + \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n    \\[7\\]\n    \n    [F. Kojima](https://scholar.google.com/scholar?btnG=&hl=en&as_sdt=0%2C23&q=author:F. Kojima), Stability and instability of the unbeatable strategy in dynamic processes, *International Journal of Economic Theory*, **2** (2006), 41-53.  doi: [10.1111/j.1365-2966.2006.0023.x.![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/crossref.jpg \"CrossRef\")](http://dx.doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2966.2006.0023.x) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Stability+and+instability+of+the+unbeatable+strategy+in+dynamic+processes+F. Kojima+2006 \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n    \\[8\\]\n    \n    [U. Schwalbe](https://scholar.google.com/scholar?btnG=&hl=en&as_sdt=0%2C23&q=author:U. Schwalbe) and [P. Walker](https://scholar.google.com/scholar?btnG=&hl=en&as_sdt=0%2C23&q=author:P. Walker), Zermelo and the early history of game theory, *Games and Economic Behavior*, **34** (2001), 123-137.  doi: [10.1006/game.2000.0794.![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/crossref.jpg \"CrossRef\")](http://dx.doi.org/10.1006/game.2000.0794) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/math-review.gif \"math-review\")](https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=MR1895174&return=pdf) [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Zermelo+and+the+early+history+of+game+theory+U. Schwalbe+2001 \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n    \\[9\\]\n    \n    E. Zermelo, Über eine Anwendung der Mengenlehre auf die Theorie des Schachspiels, in *Proceedings of the Fifth International Congress of Mathematicians (Cambridge 1912)*, (eds. E. W. Hobson and A. E. H. Love), Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, 2 (1913), 501-504. [![](https://www.aimsciences.org/style/web/images/custom/scholar.png \"scholar\")](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=E.+Zermelo,+Über+eine+Anwendung+der+Mengenlehre+auf+die+Theorie+des+Schachspiels,+in+Proceedings+of+the+Fifth+International+Congress+of+Mathematicians+\\(Cambridge+1912\\),+\\(eds.+E.+W.+Hobson+and+A.+E.+H.+Love\\),+Cambridge+University+Press,+Cambridge,+2+\\(1913\\),+501-504. + \"Go to article in Google Scholar\")\n    \n\n[Access History](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n-   ### Access History\n    \n    ![加载中](/style/web/images/article/1.gif)\n    \n-   \n\n[PDF](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n[XML](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n[Export Citation](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n\n###### SHARE\n\n[Email to a Friend](mailto:?Subject=On Zermelo's theorem&Body=An AIMS publication is recommended to you.  For more information see URL: https://www.aimsciences.org/article/id/6ec22007-b4e5-49f1-a59a-153cf9f1c420)\n\n![](/style/web/images/custom/share_facebook.png)\n\n![](/style/web/images/custom/share_twitter.png)\n\n![](/style/web/images/custom/share_linkin.png)\n\n![](/style/web/images/custom/share_mendeley.png)\n\n![](/style/web/images/custom/share_researchGate.png)\n\n## Article Metrics\n\nHTML views(8122) PDF downloads(198) Cited by(0)\n\n[![](/style/web/images/trend_03.jpg)](#trendmd-suggestions)\n\n[\n\n###### Access History\n\n![](/style/web/images/Access-list_03.jpg)\n\n](#Access-list)\n\n## Other Articles By Authors\n\n-   on this site\n    -   [Rabah Amir](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n    -   [Igor V. Evstigneev](javascript:void\\(0\\);)\n-   on Google Scholar\n    -   [Rabah Amir](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Rabah Amir)\n    -   [Igor V. Evstigneev](http://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Igor V. Evstigneev)\n\n**Top**\n\n### Catalog\n\n×Close\n\n## **Export File**\n\n#### Ci